From: minisandbox <minisandbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] x86/boot: map PVM decompression output before events exist

The 64-bit decompressor replaces the loader's identity page tables before
PVM has registered its PVCS and event entry.  Its normal demand-fault mapping
therefore cannot service the first write to the decompression output range.
Carry that range into the replacement identity map explicitly for PVM.

diff --git a/arch/x86/boot/compressed/misc.c b/arch/x86/boot/compressed/misc.c
--- a/arch/x86/boot/compressed/misc.c
+++ b/arch/x86/boot/compressed/misc.c
@@ -479,6 +479,15 @@ asmlinkage __visible void *extract_kernel(void *rmode, unsigned char *output)
 		error("Destination virtual address changed when not relocatable");
 #endif
 
+	/*
+	 * minisandbox: initialize_identity_maps() replaced the bootloader's
+	 * complete init_size mapping. PVM cannot use the decompressor's #PF
+	 * demand mapper until its event entry and PVCS have been registered.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PVM_GUEST) && pvm_detected)
+		kernel_add_identity_map((unsigned long)output,
+					(unsigned long)output + needed_size);
+
 	debug_putstr("\nDecompressing Linux... ");
 
 	if (init_unaccepted_memory()) {
-- 
2.43.0
